msm: work around liuqin's dark first modeset with delayed display cycles.

This is a temporary, board-specific workaround for the U-Boot hand-off path.
The proper fix is to stop the inherited display pipeline before the kernel's
first modeset; the probe-time teardown is still to be implemented.

The bootloader leaves this board's display pipeline running -- ABL's splash,
then U-Boot's menu -- and the first modeset that takes it over does not
produce a picture: the CRTC ends up active, the panel runs its init sequence
(the same 198 DSI commands that work later), the framebuffer holds the
console text and DPMS is on, yet the panel stays dark.  A stop/start cycle
of the pipeline brings it up, and it stays up from then on.

Measured on liuqin (mainline 7.2.5, fbdev DRM client, ABL/U-Boot hand-off),
with the port's userspace boot service and every mask option absent:

  - writing 1 then 0 to /sys/class/graphics/fb0/blank in the running system
    brings the panel up;
  - the same cycle run inline from the msm probe, right after the in-kernel
    fbdev client's first modeset, does not;
  - a single cycle from a work item four seconds later did not either;
  - cycles later in the boot, and any cycle once the system is up, do.

Which moment the panel starts accepting the cycle is not known, so retry a
few times across the boot rather than betting on one delay: five attempts
four seconds apart, the first six seconds after the fbdev client's first
modeset, stopping early as soon as userspace owns the display (after that
the DPMS commits are refused with -EBUSY, which drm_fb_helper_blank() drops
on the floor).

fb_blank() is what the userspace cure reaches: the driver's fb_blank plus
the FB_EVENT_BLANK notifier chain, so fbcon blanks and redraws too.

TODO: this timer loop is a workaround.  Investigate a kernel-side quiesce
before the first modeset: stop inherited DPU timing and both DSI streams,
then run the panel's normal reset/prepare sequence.  If that is insufficient,
test ABL's fuller DisableDisplay() power/clock teardown.  The exact hardware
state responsible is still unknown; see docs/PORTING-NOTES.md, Display
section, "Not done", for the hypothesis and acceptance test.

TODO: while this retry loop remains, tie the delayed work to the DRM device's
lifetime.  Move the work item and attempt counter into struct msm_drm_private,
initialize them before scheduling, and have the callback obtain that struct
with container_of() instead of using the current global drm_device pointer.
Call cancel_delayed_work_sync() at the start of msm_drm_uninit(), before
drm_dev_unregister() can destroy the fbdev client, including the init-failure
path.  Check fb_blank() results so a failed cycle is visible in the log.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c
@@ -6,11 +6,13 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/aperture.h>
+#include <linux/fb.h>
 #include <linux/kthread.h>
 #include <linux/sched/mm.h>
 #include <uapi/linux/sched/types.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
+#include <drm/drm_fb_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_mode_config.h>
 #include <drm/drm_vblank.h>
 #include <drm/clients/drm_client_setup.h>
@@ -21,6 +23,61 @@
 #include "msm_kms.h"
 #include "msm_mmu.h"
 
+/*
+ * Temporary liuqin workaround for a dark first modeset.
+ * The bootloader leaves the display pipeline running (ABL's splash, then
+ * U-Boot's menu), and the first modeset that takes it over does not produce a
+ * picture on this board: the CRTC ends up active, the panel runs its init
+ * sequence, the framebuffer holds the console text and DPMS is on, yet the
+ * panel stays dark.  A stop/start cycle of the pipeline brings it up and it
+ * stays up.
+ *
+ * Measured on liuqin: a single cycle at ~4-7 s after the first modeset did
+ * not take; cycles later in the boot (and any cycle once the system is up)
+ * did.  Which moment the panel starts accepting the cycle is not known, so
+ * retry a few times across the boot instead of betting on one delay -- five
+ * attempts four seconds apart, the first six seconds after the fbdev client's
+ * first modeset, and stopping as soon as userspace owns the display (the DPMS
+ * commits are refused with -EBUSY after that, and drm_fb_helper_blank()
+ * drops that on the floor).
+ *
+ * The schedule is a compromise measured on the unit: with attempts at roughly
+ * 6, 10, 14, 18 and 22 s after the first modeset, the panel lit between 10 and
+ * 20 s.  The first attempt was still too early on the measured boots.  Every
+ * attempt is a visible dark second (the cycle is a real POWERDOWN/UNBLANK), so
+ * early, repeated attempts can make the user see the panel blink after it is
+ * already up.
+ *
+ * fb_blank() is what the userspace cure reaches (the driver's fb_blank plus
+ * the FB_EVENT_BLANK notifier chain, so fbcon blanks and redraws as well).
+ */
+static struct delayed_work liuqin_panel_cycle_work;
+static struct drm_device *liuqin_panel_cycle_dev;
+static int liuqin_panel_cycle_attempts = 5;
+
+static void liuqin_panel_cycle(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct drm_device *ddev = liuqin_panel_cycle_dev;
+	struct fb_info *info;
+
+	if (!ddev || liuqin_panel_cycle_attempts <= 0)
+		return;
+
+	info = ddev->fb_helper ? ddev->fb_helper->info : NULL;
+	if (!info || ddev->master) {
+		liuqin_panel_cycle_attempts = 0;
+		return;
+	}
+
+	pr_info("liuqin: panel cycle #%d\n", 6 - liuqin_panel_cycle_attempts);
+	fb_blank(info, FB_BLANK_POWERDOWN);
+	fb_blank(info, FB_BLANK_UNBLANK);
+
+	if (--liuqin_panel_cycle_attempts)
+		schedule_delayed_work(&liuqin_panel_cycle_work,
+				      msecs_to_jiffies(4000));
+}
+
 static const struct drm_mode_config_funcs mode_config_funcs = {
 	.fb_create = msm_framebuffer_create,
 	.atomic_check = msm_atomic_check,
@@ -385,4 +441,11 @@
 
 	drm_kms_helper_poll_init(ddev);
 	drm_client_setup(ddev, NULL);
+
+	if (ddev->fb_helper && ddev->fb_helper->info) {
+		liuqin_panel_cycle_dev = ddev;
+		INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&liuqin_panel_cycle_work, liuqin_panel_cycle);
+		schedule_delayed_work(&liuqin_panel_cycle_work,
+				      msecs_to_jiffies(6000));
+	}
 }
